{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.loci_disjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.loci_disjoint","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/EmGermMomentVanishing.lean#L169-L175","doc":"The two distinguished loci are **distinct** whenever `2 ≠ 0`: the moment\ncannot vanish and degenerate at the same `q`. So \"sterile\" and \"undefined\" are\ngenuinely different failure modes of the germ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.qInt2_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.qInt2_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/EmGermMomentVanishing.lean#L157-L167","doc":"**`[2]_q` vanishes exactly at `q² = −1`.** In particular `[2]_i = 0`, so the\nmoment is undefined at the discrete `q = i` point rather than merely small\nthere. Recorded as a coincidence of loci with the measure wall's stated\n`q = i` no-germ obstruction; the identification is not proved here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.sterile_iff_bar_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.sterile_iff_bar_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/EmGermMomentVanishing.lean#L145-L153","doc":"**Sterility and symmetric braiding are the same condition.** The moment\nvanishes iff `h = 0`, which is the very factor whose vanishing makes\n`tr σ⁻¹ = tr σ` in `TraceSignFlipRegime.trace_sign_flip_iff_symmetric`. So the\nEM germ is non-sterile *because* the braiding is non-symmetric — the two facts\nare one fact, and the deuteron's single-generator sterility is a genuinely\ndifferent mechanism (abelian transport), not this one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.emMoment_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.emMoment_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/EmGermMomentVanishing.lean#L132-L143","doc":"**The moment vanishes exactly at `q² = 1`.** Away from the degenerate locus\n`[2]_q = 0`, the germ's EM-singlet channel is sterile precisely at the\nclassical / self-dual point and nowhere else — so non-sterility is generic, not\na lucky sample point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.barOddGen_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.barOddGen_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/EmGermMomentVanishing.lean#L123-L130","doc":"`h = 0` exactly on the bar-fixed locus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.emMoment_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.emMoment_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/EmGermMomentVanishing.lean#L115-L119","doc":"**The moment is bar-odd**: `m_F(q⁻¹) = −m_F(q)`. Bar-odd over bar-even is\nbar-odd, so the moment reverses under `q ↦ q⁻¹` — the signature of a genuine\n`q`-motion rather than a static invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.qInt2_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.qInt2_inv","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/EmGermMomentVanishing.lean#L111-L113","doc":"`[2]_q` is bar-even: `[2]_{q⁻¹} = [2]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.barOddGen_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.barOddGen_inv","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/EmGermMomentVanishing.lean#L107-L109","doc":"`h` is bar-odd: `h(q⁻¹) = −h(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.emMoment_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.emMoment_eq","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/EmGermMomentVanishing.lean#L95-L103","doc":"The audit's two spellings of the moment are the same object:\n`−h/[2]_q = −(q² − 1)/(q² + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.qInt2_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.qInt2_eq","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/EmGermMomentVanishing.lean#L91-L93","doc":"`[2]_q = (q² + 1)/q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.barOddGen_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.barOddGen_eq","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/EmGermMomentVanishing.lean#L87-L89","doc":"`h = (q² − 1)/q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.emMoment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.emMoment","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/EmGermMomentVanishing.lean#L81-L83","doc":"The EM-singlet moment of the germ curvature, in the closed form the probe\nmeasured: `m_F = −h/[2]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.qInt2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.qInt2","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/EmGermMomentVanishing.lean#L78-L79","doc":"The bar-even quantum integer `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.barOddGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.EmGermMomentVanishing.barOddGen","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/EmGermMomentVanishing.lean#L68-L76","doc":"The bar-odd generator `h = q − q⁻¹`. Vanishes exactly on the bar-fixed\nlocus `q² = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}